---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const faqSchema = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What happens to my current hosting?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Your site moves to my infrastructure. Once everything's verified and running, you cancel your old hosting. I handle the full migration. DNS, files, database, email routing. Zero downtime."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I still have access to my site?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Absolutely. You keep full WordPress admin access. Log in, edit content, publish posts, whatever you need. I handle the infrastructure and the stuff that requires technical knowledge."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What if I want to leave?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It's month-to-month after onboarding. No lock-in. If you leave, I'll give you a full backup and 30 days to migrate elsewhere. Your site is always yours."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What about my domain and email?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Your domain stays yours. I never take ownership. Email routing is preserved during migration. If you're on shared hosting email, I'll help you set up something proper that won't break when the hosting changes."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do maintenance hours roll over?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "They don't. Hours are use-it-or-lose-it each month. Keeps pricing predictable for both of us. If you consistently need more, we'll adjust your tier. Consistently need fewer, same thing."
      }
    }
  ]
});
---

<Base title="Web Management | Managed WordPress Hosting & Security" description="Managed WordPress hosting, security, updates, and monthly reporting. Your site lives on my infrastructure.">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqSchema} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Services","item":"https://codyasmith.com/services"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Web Management","item":"https://codyasmith.com/services/web-management"}]})} />
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative pt-40 pb-24 px-6 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute top-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-[600px] h-[400px] bg-amber-500/5 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/services" class="reveal inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-neutral-500 text-sm hover:text-neutral-300 transition-colors duration-300 mb-8 group">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 group-hover:-translate-x-1 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M7 16l-4-4m0 0l4-4m-4 4h18" />
        </svg>
        All services
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
        <span class="reveal text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em]">01</span>
        <div class="reveal gradient-divider flex-1"></div>
      </div>
      <h1 class="reveal font-serif text-5xl md:text-7xl text-neutral-100 leading-[1.05] mb-6">
        Web Management
      </h1>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-500 italic text-sm tracking-wide mb-10">Your site lives on my infrastructure.</p>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl" data-frame="default">
        I ask clients who hosts their website. Most of them don't know. They think it's GoDaddy but they're not sure. Nobody's logged in since the last developer left. The SSL certificate expired two months ago and nobody noticed until a customer mentioned the warning screen. That's the moment I usually get the call.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
        Your website should be the one thing that just works. Dedicated cloud hosting, managed security, daily backups, proactive monitoring, all under one roof. You focus on the business. I make sure the site keeps up with it.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
        I ask clients who hosts their website. Most of them don't know. The SSL expired two months ago and a customer mentioned the warning screen before anyone on staff noticed. The last developer left and took the credentials. That's the moment I usually get the call.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mt-6">
        What I run for clients is WordPress. WordPress where it earns its keep. Something simpler where it doesn't.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 surface-1">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-16">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Process</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">Here's what happens.</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl" data-vibe="default">
          Your site moves to my infrastructure. I take over the hosting, the security, the updates, and the monitoring. You stop thinking about it.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-vibe="beach">
          Your competitors' sites are faster, more secure, and better maintained. That's not a guess. It's what I see every time I audit a new client's hosting. This is how you close that gap.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-vibe="mountain">
          I take over the infrastructure, keep it alive, and send you proof every month that it's handled. Server configuration, security hardening, update testing, backup verification, all documented, all mine.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="relative">
        <!-- Vertical line -->
        <div class="absolute left-6 md:left-8 top-0 bottom-0 w-px bg-gradient-to-b from-amber-500/40 via-amber-500/20 to-transparent"></div>

        <div class="space-y-16">
          <div class="reveal relative pl-16 md:pl-20">
            <div class="absolute left-3 md:left-5 top-1 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500 bg-neutral-950 flex items-center justify-center">
              <span class="text-amber-400 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">1</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">I move everything.</h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-frame="default">
              DNS, hosting, email routing, plugins, database. Your site comes off whatever shared box it's been sitting on and onto dedicated cloud infrastructure under my management. Zero downtime. You don't touch anything. You don't even notice it happened, except the site gets faster.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
              Off the shared box, onto cloud infrastructure that can grow with you. Faster pages. Headroom for traffic spikes. The site stops being a constraint and starts being a foundation.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
              I move everything off the shared box that's been one bad neighbor away from a problem. DNS, email, plugins, database, all migrated under my management with zero downtime and a written record of every change.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="reveal relative pl-16 md:pl-20">
            <div class="absolute left-3 md:left-5 top-1 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500/60 bg-neutral-950 flex items-center justify-center">
              <span class="text-amber-400/60 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">2</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">I take the thing apart.</h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-frame="default">
              Plugin conflicts, outdated dependencies, security holes, performance problems nobody told you about. Everything gets documented. This becomes your first Site Health Report and the baseline for everything that comes after.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
              I take the site apart and find what's slowing it down, what's redundant, what's underused. The fixes compound from there: faster site, leaner stack, more headroom for the things you actually want to do.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
              A diagnostic teardown of the whole stack. Plugin conflicts, dependencies, security gaps, performance issues, all documented. Nothing on the site is undocumented after this.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="reveal relative pl-16 md:pl-20">
            <div class="absolute left-3 md:left-5 top-1 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500/40 bg-neutral-950 flex items-center justify-center">
              <span class="text-amber-400/40 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">3</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">Then it starts pulling its weight.</h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-frame="default">
              Updates get tested before they touch your live site. Security monitoring runs around the clock. Backups happen daily. And when something breaks, because eventually something always does, my phone buzzes. Not yours.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
              Stable infrastructure that lets the business move faster. The site stops being the bottleneck. You ship the campaign, push the page, run the promotion. The site keeps up.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
              Updates tested in staging, logged, deployed. Security monitoring with alerts. Daily backups with point-in-time restore. When something breaks, the incident is documented end to end. Your phone stays quiet.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="reveal relative pl-16 md:pl-20">
            <div class="absolute left-3 md:left-5 top-1 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500/20 bg-neutral-950 flex items-center justify-center">
              <span class="text-amber-400/20 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">4</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">First of every month, the report lands.</h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-frame="default">
              Plain language. What I did, what I found, what's coming next, and how performance compares to last month. You never have to wonder if the money's doing anything. The report is the receipt.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
              Every month, a clear read on where the site is gaining ground: load times trending down, Core Web Vitals improving, security clean, work queued. You see what's improving and decide what to push on next.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
              First of every month, a written report lands. What I did, what I found, what's coming, with month-over-month comparisons. The receipt for the work, in your inbox, in writing.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What's included -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 dot-grid">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-16">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Coverage</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">What's covered.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 reveal-stagger">
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6" style="--i:0">
          <div class="text-amber-400 mb-4">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M5 12h14M5 12a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h14a2 2 0 012 2v4a2 2 0 01-2 2M5 12a2 2 0 00-2 2v4a2 2 0 002 2h14a2 2 0 002-2v-4a2 2 0 00-2-2" /></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Cloud hosting</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">Dedicated cloud server. Not shared with hundreds of other sites. Fast, isolated, and fully under my control.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">Your site gets its own server: fast, stable, and built to grow with your business.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">Dedicated VPS with isolated resources, SSD storage, server-level caching, and manual configuration. No shared hosting neighbors.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6" style="--i:1">
          <div class="text-amber-400 mb-4">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M12 15v2m-6 4h12a2 2 0 002-2v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2zm10-10V7a4 4 0 00-8 0v4h8z" /></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Security</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">SSL certificates, firewall, malware scanning, login hardening. Problems caught before you know they exist.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">Layered security that keeps threats out so you never have to think about them.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">SSL provisioning, WAF rules, brute-force protection, file integrity monitoring, and weekly malware scans with automated alerting.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6" style="--i:2">
          <div class="text-amber-400 mb-4">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M4 4v5h.582m15.356 2A8.001 8.001 0 004.582 9m0 0H9m11 11v-5h-.581m0 0a8.003 8.003 0 01-15.357-2m15.357 2H15" /></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Updates</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">WordPress core, themes, and plugins. Tested in staging first. No "update all and pray" approach.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">Updates handled the way they should be: tested before they touch your live site. You never see the broken version.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">WordPress core, theme, and plugin updates are staged, regression-tested, screenshotted, and deployed with a rollback plan in place. No "update all and pray."</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6" style="--i:3">
          <div class="text-amber-400 mb-4">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M4 7v10c0 2.21 3.582 4 8 4s8-1.79 8-4V7M4 7c0 2.21 3.582 4 8 4s8-1.79 8-4M4 7c0-2.21 3.582-4 8-4s8 1.79 8 4" /></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Daily backups</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">Automated daily. Point-in-time restoration. If something goes wrong, we roll back in minutes, not days.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">The site can always go back to the way it was yesterday. That's the floor.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">Automated daily snapshot of files and database. 30-day retention, off-site storage, point-in-time restore tested every quarter. Disaster recovery is not theoretical.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6" style="--i:4">
          <div class="text-amber-400 mb-4">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M9 19v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2zm0 0V9a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v10m-6 0a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v14a2 2 0 01-2 2h-2a2 2 0 01-2-2z" /></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Uptime monitoring</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">Checked every 60 seconds. If your site goes down, I know before your customers do.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">If the site goes down, I know about it before your customers do. They almost never see a downtime moment that wasn't planned.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">UptimeRobot probes the site every 60 seconds from multiple regions. Alerts route to me by SMS and email within seconds of any failed check. Public status data available on request.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6" style="--i:5">
          <div class="text-amber-400 mb-4">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M9 17v-2m3 2v-4m3 4v-6m2 10H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z" /></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Site Health Report</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">Monthly. What happened, what's next, how performance compares. The proof that the work gets done.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">The work is visible every month. You never have to wonder if the retainer is earning its keep.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">Monthly written deliverable with sections for completed work, identified issues, Core Web Vitals trend, uptime metric, security log summary, and next-cycle priorities. Comparable month over month.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Portal block: where the engagement lives -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-12 text-center">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">The portal</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">The receipt for the engagement.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal glow-card p-8 md:p-10">
        <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-lg" data-frame="default">
          Every engagement runs through one portal: contracts, change orders, invoices, files, milestones, approvals, notifications. One log-in, one source of truth, one place to find anything I've ever done for you.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-lg" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
          The portal puts the engagement on rails. Approvals move faster, milestones land cleaner, and the work compounds because nothing's stuck waiting for someone to chase it down.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-lg" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
          The portal is the receipt for the engagement. Contracts, change orders, invoices, approvals, every milestone, every file. Nothing the engagement produces lives in a thread you'd lose.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-lg mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-white/5" style="display:none" data-vibe="mountain">
          Magic-link sign-in (no passwords to leak). Sessions hashed. Files in encrypted storage. Activity log behind every action. Your data stays yours, end to end.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Mid-page CTA -->
  <section class="py-16 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center reveal">
      <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm mb-4">Sound like what you need?</p>
      <a href="/contact?interest=web-management" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-4 border border-white/10 text-neutral-300 font-medium text-sm rounded-lg hover:border-amber-500/25 hover:text-amber-400 transition-all duration-300">
        Let's talk about your site
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pricing (calibrated, no public tier ladder until ecosystem routing exists) -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 surface-1">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Pricing</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100 mb-8">Calibrated, not off the rack.</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-10">
          Pricing is calibrated to your site. A 20-page brochure site doesn't carry the same maintenance load as a 120-page lead-generation engine. Tell me what you're running and I'll show you what fits.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact?interest=web-management" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-4 bg-amber-500 text-neutral-950 font-semibold text-sm rounded-lg hover:bg-amber-400 transition-all duration-300 hover:shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(245,158,11,0.25)]">
          Tell me about your site
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-16">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Questions</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">Things people ask.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4 reveal-stagger">
        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:0">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            What happens to my current hosting?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            It moves to mine. I handle DNS, files, database, email routing. Once everything's running and you've confirmed it, you cancel the old account. Zero downtime. Most clients don't even realize the switch happened until they see the speed difference.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:1">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            Do I still have access to my site?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Yes. Full WordPress admin. Log in, edit content, publish posts. It's your site. I handle the engine room. You keep the keys to the front door.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:2">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            What if I want to leave?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Month-to-month after onboarding. No contracts, no lock-in. If you leave, I hand you a full backup and give you 30 days to land somewhere else. I don't hold sites hostage. That's the other guy's move.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:3">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            What about my domain and email?
